t inside  many times I'd just hammer the key and  hope for the best  I'll keep an ear out for any refilling  audio cue between the sounds of gunshots  screams or Mick Gordon's tasty riffs  as I progress do maternal really started  to drive home the lessons that could be  found in the new prevalence that is at  the core of a game never before was it  more important to make the most of  healing glory kills flame belching for  Allah or bisecting imps for ammunition  but at the same time it wasn't this hard  previously I become reliant on the  lights and beeps of my HUD to tell me  when each ability was ready to let rip  but in losing the capacity to keep track  of my abilities I started to find little  wrinkles in the game that I could use to  my advantage sure I don't have an ammo  counter but the weapon wheel is still  usable so I could rely on holding my  weapon button to check how much plasma  of white full of rocket ammunition I had  and this was the beginning of me trying  to break the game for my own benefit as  you're selecting your weapon the time  around you slows to a crawl and I didn't  realize that I could hold that  infinitely that meant I had a little  time dilation realm that I could use not  only check ammo and select my weapon but  also to take stock of what was around me  and weigh up how to approach the zombies  and imps in front of me I really did  have to think about things a lot more  than I did in my previous playthrough  secret areas were now so much more  valuable as each upgrade extra life or  even resupply meant way more than it  ever did before glory kills were so much  more important now and instead of  jumping bladed fist first towards  whatever glowing enemy was nearby I had  to save them or stack them in groups so  I'd have a health pool to chow down on  if I needed them for a rainy day now if  you ask me a few days ago Dave how many  shots with a heavy cannon does it take  to stagger an imp and I would have said  I don't know I kind of just shut it in  till it was dead but that seemingly  innocuous piece of information was now  vital as I didn't have a clue what  resources were available to me so I had  to make the most of them so for those  wondering it takes two to three shots to  fall to a zombie and four to five an  emperor soldier and once I realized that  it almost became second nature to fire  off controlled bursts so I reliably knew  I had a living breathing demon health  care in front of me sometimes even going  against what I thought was sensible and  ignoring the real fodder to focus on the  big guys and just saving them for a  resupply - or meat hooking my way  towards them for chainsawing them in  half  and topping up my ammo supplies this new  way of playing awesome and I didn't fall  into the same habits as my previous  run-through where previously I favored  the ability to slow down time and use  the heavy canon scope to take off weak  points relying on that was now a lot  trickier mostly because apparently the  scope is part of the HUD so instead of a  sniper sight you just get a blank zoom  in great for cinematics terrible for  headshots stat man I'd try different  rooms new mods and upgrade combinations  and experience ways of playing if I  hadn't considered before I hadn't used  the saving roll room but now it was  almost essential given me one last  desperate chance not to revert the last  checkpoint this experience however has  been a bit of a double-edged sword on  one hand the combat has never felt more  intense every move mattered every step  and dooms ballet of door had to be  executed well or you were punished for  it never had the speed intensity been so  impactful but at the same time this also  meant that at the end of every arena I  was scouring for leftover supplies or  random enemies I could filter resources  which unfortunately slowed the pace of  the game for me to a noticable degree  Deemas always had an energy pushing you  forward from encounter to encounter but  now I was like some overly armed and  armored Slayer on a scavenger hunt and  I'll be honest I got stuck in an area  once or twice because I had no idea what  door had to interact with although it  may not be fair to blame the stupidity  on the game in this regard when I got to  chapter 3 though that's when things  starts to get really challenging I went  in thinking I've got all the experience  I need I've crushed the first two levels  and already have a playthrough under my  belt in the third level of the game you  get introduced to a lots of new enemies  new weapons and even more layers to the  circle of combat in Doom I felt fairly  comfortable with them previously but now  with the stakes ever higher it was  actually pretty taxing on the old gray  matter to not only keep all the layers  of gameplay in mind but also all the new  lessons doom eternal is teaching me doom  in previous years had a replication have  been some kind of mindless shooter where  you get through the game with mostly  only one or two weapons and things were  as simple as go here shoot that but  eternal has really made a lot of effort  when it comes to taking that mindless  part out and taxing your thoughts on  strategy and tactics just as much as  reactions and accuracy skills but  honestly also does that in a really  great way without you having to dial up  difficulty now to be real with you I  didn't play through the whole game in  this method I mean might be mad but I'm  not masochistic but does this way to  play create one of the coolest looking  ways to experience the game absolutely  is it really rewarding to fight through  an arena in the most cinematic way  possible hell yes honestly doom eternal  makes you feel like a bad asset every  difficulty without adding any more  layers to it basically I created my own  uphill struggle because I wanted a  challenge that I knew many others  wouldn't get and a whole purpose of a  challenge is to feel like you've  accomplished something at 